-- title:
--   Centered even base board
-- statement:
--   For a positive cycle, natural $m$, and phase residue $c$, define the even base board as the centered perturbed board with centering parameter $m$, phase $c+1$, and transposition of residues one and two. Explicitly, center the integer $c+1-ρ(i)-i$, where $ρ$ is that transposition. The definition does not assume $n=2m$ or that the board is balanced. It specifies the base values used in even single raise comparisons.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/EvenSingleRaise.lean#L10-L11

